---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// Move 4. The product, condensed. The full walkthrough lives in the methodology;
// this is the homepage version. Four checks, the sealed container, three
// verdicts, and the line that makes the verdict worth anything.
const checks = [
  { n: '01', name: 'Closed', body: 'Re-scan after the patch. Is the reported finding actually gone, or did it move?' },
  { n: '02', name: 'Hole shut', body: 'Fire attacks the fixer never saw. One that still lands is a failure.' },
  { n: '03', name: 'Behaviour held', body: 'Every ordinary input still matches a known-correct reference.' },
  { n: '04', name: 'Provenance clean', body: 'No suppression, no new finding, no alert closed while attacks still land.' },
];
---

<Section id="checks" tint>
  <h2 class="h2 reveal" style="max-width:20ch">Four checks, in a sealed container.</h2>

  <p class="reveal mt-8 text-[17px] leading-[1.6]" style="--reveal-delay:60ms;max-width:64ch">
    The patch is applied to a clean checkout and scored with no network egress, torn down
    between patches. Three of the checks are the ordinary questions any careful team asks. The
    second is the one nobody runs.
  </p>

  <ol class="reveal mt-11 grid grid-cols-1 gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-[3px] border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    {
      checks.map((ch) => (
        <li class="flex flex-col bg-bg p-6 lg:p-7">
          <span class="mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">{ch.n}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-[17px] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.012em]">{ch.name}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-2">{ch.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="mono reveal mt-8 border-l-2 border-line pl-5 text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-fg-2" style="--reveal-delay:120ms;max-width:62ch">
    If you let a student write their own exam, they will pass it. You test them on
    questions they have not seen.
  </p>

  <div class="reveal mt-11 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-6 lg:mt-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1fr)]" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    <div>
      <p class="micro mb-3">Three verdicts</p>
      <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.62]">
        <span class="text-accent">VERIFIED</span>,
        <span class="text-fail">NOT VERIFIED</span>, and
        <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE</strong>. The third is a
        first-class verdict, reported rather than dropped. A result we cannot stand behind is
        worth more than one we invent, and that is the point.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="border-t border-line pt-6 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0">
      <p class="micro mb-3">Why the verdict is worth anything</p>
      <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.62]">
        We do not write fixes. The thing being checked and the thing doing the checking are
        never the same party. Independence is the whole product.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="mono reveal mt-11 border-t border-line pt-6 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-fg-2" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    Works with any scanner and any fixer. SARIF in, verdict out.
  </p>
</Section>
